        <div class="text"><a href="/555014141/factors-affecting-the-climate-of-cities-paper">Factors Affecting the Climate of Cities Paper</a></div>
    </div>
    <div class="description">In 6 pages of text, discuss the look of the climagraphs and the factors affecting the
climate of each city. You can consider things such as: latitude, nearness to water, air
masses, atmospheric and oceanic circulation, northern or southern hemisphere, etc. In
addition, compare and contrast the factors that account for the climate differences
and/or similarities among the three cities lahore, toronto, and sydney.
Guidelines
1. The paper must be typed, double-spaced, times new roman and 12-point font.
2. The length of the paper must be 6 pages of text, excluding illustrations and
references).
3. At least 2 illustrations are required (e.g. tables, graphs, maps, diagrams). Each
illustration must be referenced, properly labeled and referred to in the text.
4. Include a title and use sub-headings to organize the essay.
5. Use correct grammar, spelling, sentences, tenses, vocabulary, paragraph construction and
punctuation. All pages must be numbered.
6. Indicate in LARGE TYPE on the title page of your paper, the course number, instructor&rsquo;s
name, your name and student number.
7. Save your file in WORD OR PDF format with your first and last names. Submit your
assignment in the Assignment Folder on D2L by clicking on &lsquo;Assessment&rsquo; and then
&lsquo;Assignment&rsquo; and upload your essay file.
References
You must reference/cite all quotes, ideas, and illustrations that are not your own using both in-
text citations and a bibliography. In-text citations appear directly in the essay to support your
argument and indicate information sources. The scientific method is required (e.g. Smith 2019;
Harris and Jones 2022, p. 3). In the bibliography section, lists in full reference all of the
information sources you referenced within the text. Use the American Psychological Association
(APA) referencing style for the bibliography at the end of the essay.
You must have a minimum of 6 references. You can use as many references as possible and
they are included in the page limit. Use journal articles, books, government publications, agency
reports, technical reports (United Nations or World Bank, World Food and Agriculture
Organization etc). Only 2 Internet sources are required. An Internet source may include, for
example, &ldquo;facts&rdquo; listed on the Statistics Canada website). DO NOT USE Wikipedia, blocs, or web
links that have no date of publication and no agency or individual names associated with the
piece, paper, or report. You are allowed to use e-books, electronic journals, government
documents and research reports. Use recent references and publications as much as possible
(eg. 2016 to 2022). You may use one older article only if it refers to historical or past activities,
events or decisions.
</div>
