        <div class="text"><a href="/973649629/heart-over-brain-a-faith-perspective">Heart Over Brain: A Faith Perspective</a></div>
    </div>
    <div class="description">Heart or Brain?  Which are you?  Please choose one.  We all use both our brains and our hearts, but likely we lean in one direction more often than the other.  If you lean in the direction of letting your heart rule, can you give a specific example from your own experience?  If you lean in the direction of letting your brain rule, can you give us a specific example from you own experience?

Also consider these questions:  (Remember, rise above &quot;I like&quot; &quot;I don't like&quot; &quot;I agree&quot; or &quot;disagree&quot; or &quot;in my opinion.&quot;) Examine the idea to better understand the issues.

Question for those who choose the heart:

1.  What are the benefits of letting the heart rule?
2.  What are the drawbacks?
3.  What adjectives or phrases would you use to describe heart-people like you?  (Make a list.)
4.  What adjectives or phrases would you use to describe brain-people?
5. Examine the adjectives and phrases you used to describe brain-people.  What assumptions, prejudices, and biases do these words show?
6. If you wanted to understand and get along with a brain-person, what strategy might you use? 
7,  How would you advise a brain-person to get along with a heart like you?

answer as if i chose the heart over the brain
include how there is no mention in the NKJV bible about the brain being tied to faith and how the heart is use specific example like romans 10:10, Acts 15:8-11, and proverbs 3:5-6 
include how According to James 4:5, the Holy Spirit came into our hearts as a Permanent Indweller meaning the heart is connected directly to our spirits </div>
