        <div class="text"><a href="/270290770/the-impact-of-social-media-misuse-on">The Impact of Social Media Misuse on Organizations and Leaders</a></div>
    </div>
    <div class="description">The Impact of Social Media Misuse on Organizations and Leaders 

  

Kenneth M. Monroe 

United States of America Drill Sergeant Academy 

Course #: 003-25 

January 28, 2025 

 

The Impact of Social Media Misuse on Organizations and Leaders 

  

The importance of social media misuse within the United States Army. The damage that may be done to an organization or leaders could be irreparable due to negligence and complacency of individuals that submit posts to social media. This could diminish the reputation of individuals and possibly the overall missions given to these organizations. Online misconduct is described as &ldquo;the use of electronic communication to inflict harm. Electronic communication is the transfer of information (signs, writing, images, sounds, or data) transmitted by computer, phone or another electronic device. Electronic communications include, but are not limited to: text messages, emails, chats, instant messaging, screensavers, blogs, social media sites, electronic device applications, and Web/video conferencing&rdquo;. In this day and age, we live in a world where information is readily accessible and capable of being distributed from anywhere in the world. This has been proven to be extremely beneficial to the United States Army. However, this could also be extremely dangerous when the wrong information is posted or obtained by our advisory or the general public. There has been a plethora of discussions held about social media use by military personnel. Topics of interest were the advantages and disadvantage of their use within our ranks. Not to mention the overall challenges of holding a fine line of what is allowed and what could be used against an organization. For advantages you have a few advantages such as; keeping military members connected, recruitment operations, and es pri d&eacute;cor. On the other you have individuals committing Operation security violations, Representing the U.S Army in social media posts which would be seen as unbecoming of a soldier, and political support while in uniform. &ldquo;Enlisted Soldiers who make derogatory or disrespectful statements about political leaders may violate Article 134 of the UCMJ when they make these comments on a social media site.&rdquo; </div>
