        <div class="icon"></div>
        <div class="text"><a href="/503155593/navigating-personal-health-decisions-an-informed-approach">Navigating Personal Health Decisions: An Informed Approach</a></div>
    </div>
    <div class="description">1. A completed Health Decisions graphic organizer
2. A two- to three-sentence review of the health solutions you chose, and your reasoning for
choosing them
Step 1: Prepare for the project.
a) Read through the guide before you begin so you know the expectations for this project.
b) If anything is not clear to you, ask your teacher for assistance.
Step 2: Conduct research.
a) Find three products, services, or preventable practices for each health issue chosen, and
complete the graphic organizer.
b) Use sites such as the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) or Consumer Reports
for product reviews, or consult a physician for more information.
c) Cite credible sources to back up your answer.
Step 3: Complete the graphic organizer provided.
a) Use your research to list and review three health solutions for each health issue.
b) Use your research to identify the most effective health solution for each health issue.
Step 4: Write summaries of the health solutions you chose.
a) Each summary should be two to three sentences long.
b) Include reasoning for your choices based on credible resources.
Student Guide (continued)
Copyright &copy; Edgenuity Inc.
Step 5: Evaluate your project using this checklist.
If you can check each box below, you are ready to submit your project.
 Did you research two of the three health issues listed in the graphic organizer?
 Did you find three health solutions for each health issue chosen?
 Did you review the effectiveness and safety of each health solution discussed?
 Did you provide credible resources for your review?
 Did you choose the best health solution to prevent or treat the health issue?
 Did you provide reasoning for your choice?
 Did you list the factors that influenced your decision?
 Did you summarize the choices you made and discuss what influenced your decision?
 Did you check and correct spelling, punctuation, and grammar throughout your document?
Step 6: Revise and submit your project.
a) If you were unable to check off all of the requirements on the checklist, go back and make
sure that your project is complete. Save your project before submitting it.
b) When you have completed your graphic organizer and summary, return to the Virtual
Classroom and use the &ldquo;Add Files&rdquo; option to locate and submit your assignment.
c) Congratulations! You have completed your project</div>
