    <div class="description">
Please respond to the following prompt question thoroughly in a 3-4 page paper written in 12-point professional-looking font (double-spaced with 1 inch margins) which follows the course policy according to which outside research is prohibited. Please make use only of the readings and videos assigned, the lectures, handouts, and the discussions we've had about them as your only resource. Each thinker we've discussed deals explicitly or implicitly with the prompt question and should be discussed in your paper--this includes Heidegger, the natural philosophers, the preSocratics, Socrates, Plato, Aristotle, and the Eastern thinkers. Look at what they have to say and think about how these thinkers might contribute to your answer, citing their work and documenting citations properly along the way where appropriate:      

Some of the handouts include heidegger's memorial address and many of the ideas can be found in the Living Philosophy 3e book by Lewis Vaughn for a PHIL1301 class</div>
